  "worked_solution": "We use the triangle law of addition to add the vectors $a$ and $b.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/a493346a118732d2b435e1757bcbabe756c5d0482aec0688c095b7151352d4c7.png)\n\nNotice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={15}^{2}+{9}^{2} \\\\  & =306\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $|a+b|=\\sqrt{306}=3\\sqrt{34}.$",
